KG42.register("clusters-3f73b12f5fb723dc0ccae4f9",{"id":"12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v142-d-K003","paper":"12-p2p_microgrid_trading","label":"Elecbay half-hour order formation, counterparty selection, and gate-closure permissions","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Elecbay half-hour order formation, counterparty selection, and gate-closure permissions","market_meaning":"Consumers and prosumers post energy demand or surplus energy for half-hour periods on Elecbay according to their buying or selling roles in the corresponding periods, establishing counterparty relationships by browsing listings and placing orders; permissions to modify orders change with gate closure and network violation conditions.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination","matching","participation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Applies to the platform descriptions for Elecbay grid-connected microgrids and LV distribution networks. Buyers browsing supply and sellers browsing demand are two order-placement paths; DSO authority after gate closure retains the prerequisite of network violations, and last on first off is retained only as an example. The Elecbay platform's reception responsibilities are not equivalent to the DSO's validation responsibilities.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Entity permissions, half-hour products, information submission, and counterparty selection jointly produce orders awaiting processing, so the assembly spans participation, bidding, matching, and coordination. The boundary ends at order formation and modification permissions; no claim is yet made that network validation or acceptance decisions have been completed. The payment content of R008 is retained in full and referenced on a shared basis in the settlement cluster.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides demand listings, order content, and demand-side gate-closure permissions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides supply listings, the seller-initiated order-placement path, and supply-side gate-closure permissions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Specifies the platform interface for submitting orders to Elecbay; its payment interface is shared with v142-d-K004."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Organizes the two listing-browsing paths as counterparty selection during order placement."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Defines the platform trading relationships available to consumers."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R012","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Supplements prosumers' trading permissions and the flexibility of peers' buying and selling roles across periods."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R013","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Provides the half-hour product scope shared by demand and supply listings."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-21"],"rationale":"The energy required for a half-hour period constitutes the product content of a demand listing; the two chains respectively describe the object of trading and the submission activity."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g01-ev-21"],"rationale":"Surplus energy for a half-hour period constitutes the product content of a supply listing and connects to selling activities during the posting and bidding stages."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-15","v141-b-g01-ev-21"],"rationale":"In the seller-initiated path, the half-hour demand listed by buyers provides the information input for sellers to browse and place orders; this connection is used only under this alternative path."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g01-ev-14"],"rationale":"Seller listings provide supply information for buyers to browse and place orders, thereby supporting counterparty selection in orders."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-15","v141-b-g01-ev-21"],"rationale":"Buyer demand listings provide information for seller-initiated counterparty selection. This path is parallel to the path in which buyers browse supply; the two cannot be inferred to be steps that must be executed consecutively."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-21"],"rationale":"Demand listings and buyer orders are submitted through Elecbay, with R008 supplementing the receiving platform; submission does not mean that an order has been accepted."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g01-ev-21"],"rationale":"Supply listings are provided through Elecbay, connecting supply submission activities with the platform's reception responsibilities, without inferring that the platform itself completes the network feasibility assessment."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L008","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-28"],"rationale":"The same platform description grants consumers and prosumers their respective trading options. The scopes of these two types of entities jointly constitute the scope of order participants, but the entity nodes are not merged."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-21","v141-b-g01-ev-28"],"rationale":"Peers' buying and selling roles across periods are compatible with the two types of listings, demand and surplus energy; each peer is not required to submit both buy and sell orders in every period."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C005","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-21","v141-b-g01-ev-23","v141-b-g01-ev-24"],"rationale":"The same arrangement of order permissions is represented separately in the demand and supply chains. The respective conditions concerning gate closure, network violations, and the example strategy are retained; shared evidence is not interpreted as indicating complete duplication of the provisions on the two sides."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R007::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R008::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R010::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-15","v141-b-g01-ev-21"],"rationale":"These references all refer to the Elecbay demand submission function, respectively serving as listings, inputs for seller browsing, platform reception, and matching inputs; all local references and their provisions are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R008::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R010::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g01-ev-21"],"rationale":"All three occurrences refer to the Elecbay supply submission function; its uses as a platform interface and for counterparty selection do not make the associated constraints or edges the same object."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G001","category":"upstream_missing","description":"There is not yet a complete frozen chain for order network validation and acceptance outcomes. ev16 lists Elecbay, the DSO, and the supplier, while ev22 specifically describes the DSO assessment one hour after gate closure; the existing submission interface is insufficient to determine the division of responsibilities among the parties and the acceptance outcomes. The related proposal v141-b-g01-prop-01 remains pending.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C005","v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R010::V::matching.counterparties"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-16","v141-b-g01-ev-22","v141-b-g01-ev-23"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-01"],"required_work":"Verify the division of validation responsibilities, network constraint criteria, and order status interfaces in the different descriptions; obtain additional Rule-Chains upstream and address pending proposals manually, without automatically treating order-placement matching as order acceptance."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G002","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The gate-closure time and transition of permissions are already retained in the provisions, but proposal v141-b-g01-prop-05 for a separate gate-closure event has not yet been approved; the submission node cannot be directly converted into a gate-closure node.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-21","v141-b-g01-ev-23"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-05"],"required_work":"Manually examine whether a dedicated event representation is needed; until then, continue referencing the frozen timing provisions without adding nodes or parameters."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"last on first off indicates only that later orders are more likely to be cancelled in the example; it does not establish the strategy actually adopted, a deterministic ordering, or tie handling.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-24"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"To formulate an executable cancellation rule, the policy actually selected and the selection conditions must be obtained; at this stage, retain the example conditions without rewriting them as deterministic deletion in reverse chronological order."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G004","category":"unverified_source","description":"All references in this cluster are used as eligible candidate support. The B source status remains unverified, and the existing C records likewise do not indicate that an independent C2 review has been conducted.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012","v141-c-R013"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-12","v141-b-g01-ev-13","v141-b-g01-ev-14","v141-b-g01-ev-15","v141-b-g01-ev-16","v141-b-g01-ev-20","v141-b-g01-ev-21","v141-b-g01-ev-23","v141-b-g01-ev-24","v141-b-g01-ev-27","v141-b-g01-ev-28"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the platform roles, the two order-placement paths, timing conditions, and example qualifications chain by chain, and examine the proposed semantic boundaries of this cluster."}]},"rule_refs":["12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R006","12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R007","12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R008","12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R010","12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R011","12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R012","12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R013"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-3fcd5e2d02ec7c3f","COMP-4fd16cbd90d234cb","COMP-739917e3869e45a6","COMP-a774da994c2ca212","COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","KG31-17d2981437295871","KG31-f563e86a7a19f2a5"]});
